Z||000009||filthyscarecrow||04-02-2001||08:04 PM||||you laugh at the flux capacitor? <BR>i did too when my friend told me this story. <P>he was late for high school one morning and the security officer caught him coming in late. he had overslept and would have been in deep sheeit, so he rubbed his hands in WD-40 and in the wheel wells of his jeep and told the guy it broke down and he had just got it fixed. the officer asked what was wrong with it and he (my friend knows a LOT about cars) told the guy that the flux capacitor had gone out. the officer sounded skeptical so my friend then proceeded to explain the inner workings of a vacuum cleaner and why this flux capacitor was so important. well, the security officer is also the assistant football coach, which is the real reason he has the security job- so he can coach football. needless to say, he bought the whole story, hook line and sinker. the security guy wrote him a pass and my friend went on his merry way. <P>it's always fun to test how stupid some people really are   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>allow me to show you my exhaust pipes...<p>[This message has been edited by filthyscarecrow (edited 04-02-2001).]||||reg||1
